    "user": "U0A6088AMM3",
    "text": "Hi Team,\n The OLake job `kapture_kafka_ticket_events_v1` (job 141, runs every 2 min) currently partitions `TICKET_EVENTS_KAFKA_TOPIC` on `event_at` (month). I want to switch the partition key to `ingested_at` (month).\nI understand this applies only to new writes going forward (Iceberg partition evolution — old files stay under the old spec, no rewrite/wipe). Can someone confirm that’s also how OLake’s “Finish” action on this edit behaves — i.e. it does a clean partition spec update and doesn’t trigger a full table recreate/resync of existing destination data?\nAlso, can someone confirm clicking *Finish* won’t clear or wipe the destination data in any way — partially or fully?",
